WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:02.534
-You look great, buddy.
You look sharp.

00:00:02.534 --> 00:00:04.267
It's great to see you, pal.
-How's it going?

00:00:04.267 --> 00:00:05.968
-How you doing?
It's going great.

00:00:05.968 --> 00:00:08.133
You've had a lot
going on these past few months.

00:00:08.133 --> 00:00:10.334
You released your new album
in September.

00:00:10.334 --> 00:00:11.701
Congratulations.
-Thank you.

00:00:11.701 --> 00:00:14.968
Number one. Not too shabby.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:14.968 --> 00:00:17.334
You also recently announced
that you had another child.

00:00:17.334 --> 00:00:19.901
Congratulations!
-Thank you, thank you.

00:00:19.901 --> 00:00:22.000
Thank you.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:25.467
-Your kids are actually heard
in the intro of the album.

00:00:25.467 --> 00:00:28.100
-Yes. Yes.
And, uh, I --

00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:33.834
Well, my 4-month was like
sort of a subliminal message.

00:00:33.834 --> 00:00:36.534
I didn't just reveal it.
You know, and most of my fans,

00:00:36.534 --> 00:00:41.334
I would say a good portion did
not pick up on the heartbeat.

00:00:41.334 --> 00:00:42.968
-Well, I don't know
how you would guess.

00:00:42.968 --> 00:00:45.467
Did people actually guess that
the heartbeat is your new baby?

00:00:45.467 --> 00:00:47.133
-I do have some fans.

00:00:47.133 --> 00:00:49.300
-One person here recognized it.

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:51.434
You knew that?
-"That's a baby!"

00:00:51.434 --> 00:00:53.200
-Yeah, that's -- I mean --

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:54.834
Well, listen.
Listen to -- The other --

00:00:54.834 --> 00:00:57.834
Your other children speak.
You'll hear after --

00:00:57.834 --> 00:00:59.534
After you hear "Dada," listen.

00:00:59.534 --> 00:01:02.834
[ Child fusses ]

00:01:02.834 --> 00:01:04.100
Dada!

00:01:04.100 --> 00:01:07.100
[ Heart beating ]

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:09.067
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:09.067 --> 00:01:11.601
Now --
Do you have kids?

00:01:11.601 --> 00:01:12.834
-Yes, I do.
-Have kids. Okay.

00:01:12.834 --> 00:01:14.267
Maybe you could
give me some advice.

00:01:14.267 --> 00:01:16.334
My 4-year-old, Valentino --

00:01:16.334 --> 00:01:19.234
You know how there's
a philosophy that kids

00:01:19.234 --> 00:01:20.601
are a product
of their environment?

00:01:20.601 --> 00:01:23.868
-Yeah.
-That's not necessarily true.

00:01:23.868 --> 00:01:27.667
You know, our household,
nothing but love, great energy.

00:01:27.667 --> 00:01:30.567
And he's extremely misbehaved.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:30.567 --> 00:01:33.234
Like -- But, you know,
we get complaints from school.

00:01:33.234 --> 00:01:36.300
He has this infamous line.
He's like, "Yo no quiero tu,"

00:01:36.300 --> 00:01:38.534
which means, "I don't want you."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:38.534 --> 00:01:40.667
And it's -- it's pretty bad.
It's pretty bad.

00:01:40.667 --> 00:01:42.133
-Really?
-Yeah, yeah.

00:01:42.133 --> 00:01:45.367
-He's gonna be fine.
He's got you as a dad.

00:01:45.367 --> 00:01:47.000
Come on, bud.
Can we talk about --

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:49.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:49.968 --> 00:01:53.501
The "Fórmula" albums.
They're fantastic.

00:01:53.501 --> 00:01:55.067
The last one was on
the Billboard charts for

00:01:55.067 --> 00:01:58.767
400-and-something -- 420 weeks
or something crazy.

00:01:58.767 --> 00:02:00.467
-Yeah, something like that.
-Is that unbelievable?

00:02:00.467 --> 00:02:03.100
You got "Vol. 3."

00:02:03.100 --> 00:02:05.334
Great collaborations.

00:02:05.334 --> 00:02:10.467
I don't want to name names,
but Justin Timberlake.

00:02:10.467 --> 00:02:11.968
Whatever.
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:02:11.968 --> 00:02:13.901
I --

00:02:13.901 --> 00:02:15.434
What was Justin like?

00:02:15.434 --> 00:02:18.000
-Oh, man. What an experience.
A great experience.

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:23.100
I could tell you that prior
to showing him the record,

00:02:23.100 --> 00:02:25.534
I thought he was just going to
lay down vocals, you know,

00:02:25.534 --> 00:02:27.968
probably change
a few verses, melodies.

00:02:27.968 --> 00:02:29.734
This guy just, you know,

00:02:29.734 --> 00:02:32.133
dissected the song
and reproduced it

00:02:32.133 --> 00:02:35.300
and was telling me
how to sing the song,

00:02:35.300 --> 00:02:37.334
and he made it much better.
So he's --

00:02:37.334 --> 00:02:39.334
-He's kind of amazing.
-A true producer.

00:02:39.334 --> 00:02:40.868
-He's a magician, right?
-A true producer.

00:02:40.868 --> 00:02:43.200
-He goes, "No, do that
and do that."

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:45.234
I mean, we've done bits
with him on the show,

00:02:45.234 --> 00:02:46.467
and, yeah, he's a --
he's a perfectionist.

00:02:46.467 --> 00:02:49.000
-Shout-out to J.T.
-Shout-out to J.T.

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:51.067
Golf champion Justin Timberlake.

00:02:51.067 --> 00:02:53.067
[ Cheers and applause ]
I'll tell you...

00:02:53.067 --> 00:02:56.567
Also, there's some -- there's
some great comedians.

00:02:56.567 --> 00:02:58.267
Katt Williams.
-Yes.

00:02:58.267 --> 00:03:00.801
-Why did you decide
to put comedians on the album?

00:03:00.801 --> 00:03:02.801
-I mean, it's just, uh...

00:03:02.801 --> 00:03:05.133
It's -- I love comedy.
-Yeah.

00:03:05.133 --> 00:03:07.868
-I wanted to make it
very personal.

00:03:07.868 --> 00:03:09.534
I started
with "Fórmula, Vol. 1."

00:03:09.534 --> 00:03:12.300
I had George Lopez,
"Vol. 2," I had Kevin Hart.

00:03:12.300 --> 00:03:15.300
I just wanted to continue
with the same concept.

00:03:15.300 --> 00:03:18.067
-Yeah. Is this the
last of the "Fórmula" albums,

00:03:18.067 --> 00:03:19.133
or will there be a "Fórmula" --

00:03:19.133 --> 00:03:20.100
-Hell yeah, hell yeah,
hell yeah.

00:03:20.100 --> 00:03:21.434
This is --
[ Laughter ]

00:03:21.434 --> 00:03:23.667
You know, my fans, if I have any
fans in the audience...

00:03:23.667 --> 00:03:26.334
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:26.334 --> 00:03:30.367
Listen, you guys enjoy
the albums, and, you know,

00:03:30.367 --> 00:03:31.601
the support is amazing.

00:03:31.601 --> 00:03:34.133
I respect that you embrace me
the way you do,

00:03:34.133 --> 00:03:36.167
but a lot of work
goes into this.

00:03:36.167 --> 00:03:37.567
[ Laughter ]
And it's very stressful.

00:03:37.567 --> 00:03:39.434
-But I mean, I'm saying,
"Fórmula," if there is

00:03:39.434 --> 00:03:41.334
a "Vol. 4," there's --

00:03:41.334 --> 00:03:42.868
there's other comedians
out there that would love --

00:03:42.868 --> 00:03:46.367
-No, Sure. But a lot of work
goes into this.

00:03:46.367 --> 00:03:48.501
-I understand a lot of work,
but it's not that hard.

00:03:48.501 --> 00:03:49.901
You know, when you get
the right --

00:03:49.901 --> 00:03:52.601
you get the right comedian,
get in there, you're in and out.

00:03:52.601 --> 00:03:54.334
People want to see it.

00:03:54.334 --> 00:03:56.701
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:56.701 --> 00:03:57.934
You know, I do want to ask you,

00:03:57.934 --> 00:03:59.801
because you're very --
always been great to us

00:03:59.801 --> 00:04:02.267
and very nice to us
and very humbled

00:04:02.267 --> 00:04:04.567
and have a great team,
as well, when you come.

00:04:04.567 --> 00:04:05.934
We love everybody here.

00:04:05.934 --> 00:04:08.601
But how do you do that
when you sell out

00:04:08.601 --> 00:04:11.901
Yankee Stadium and stuff?
I mean, that's insane.

00:04:11.901 --> 00:04:14.267
-You know, there's a lot of,
like, prep and --

00:04:14.267 --> 00:04:17.033
and, you know, orchestrating,
like, these type of shows

00:04:17.033 --> 00:04:19.100
so you don't get to
really, like --

00:04:19.100 --> 00:04:20.634
you're not, you know,
on stage like,

00:04:20.634 --> 00:04:22.534
"Oh, I sold this out.
Wow. 60,000 --"

00:04:22.534 --> 00:04:24.434
Doesn't work that way, you know?
-No.

00:04:24.434 --> 00:04:27.434
But do you miss New York
when you go on the road?

00:04:27.434 --> 00:04:29.901
-I do very much.
Very much.

00:04:29.901 --> 00:04:31.968
-Yeah. What's -- What's --
What things

00:04:31.968 --> 00:04:33.934
of New York do you really miss?

00:04:33.934 --> 00:04:37.133
-This is going to sound funny,
but the food, you know?

00:04:37.133 --> 00:04:39.300
I love the food.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:39.300 --> 00:04:41.467
And I love Chinese food.

00:04:41.467 --> 00:04:45.100
And my issue is that they don't
have the same duck sauce

00:04:45.100 --> 00:04:47.167
that we have here in New York.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:47.167 --> 00:04:49.234
They don't. They don't.
-In the packets?

00:04:49.234 --> 00:04:51.801
-So I travel
with my own duck sauce.

00:04:51.801 --> 00:04:52.934
[ Laughter ]
Yeah.

00:04:52.934 --> 00:04:55.133
-You travel
with your own duck sauce.

00:04:55.133 --> 00:04:56.334
-Like, I'm not --
I'm not kidding.

00:04:56.334 --> 00:04:58.567
Like, this is real [bleep]
you know?

00:04:58.567 --> 00:05:01.667
[ Laughter ]

00:05:01.667 --> 00:05:03.334
I'm ready.
I'm ready.

00:05:03.334 --> 00:05:06.701
-So, this is --
You get th--

00:05:06.701 --> 00:05:08.868
This is the real duck sauce
that you get from

00:05:08.868 --> 00:05:11.534
your favorite Chinese restaurant
here in New York City?

00:05:11.534 --> 00:05:12.801
-Yes.
-And you travel with it.

00:05:12.801 --> 00:05:14.267
You actually have
a bag backstage,

00:05:14.267 --> 00:05:15.701
a ziplock bag,
full of duck sauce.

00:05:15.701 --> 00:05:17.267
-This is true.
I'm not making this up.

00:05:17.267 --> 00:05:20.267
I like to travel with my own
duck sauce and my own ketchup.

00:05:20.267 --> 00:05:21.501
-And your own ketchup.
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:05:21.501 --> 00:05:23.634
-I love that you travel
with the duck sauce.

00:05:23.634 --> 00:05:26.501
I just figured, since you're on
your world tour right now,

00:05:26.501 --> 00:05:28.234
you are bringing it
to the States, as well,

00:05:28.234 --> 00:05:29.634
back to America...
-Yes, yes.

00:05:29.634 --> 00:05:31.033
-...I wanted to make sure
that you're going to be okay.

00:05:31.033 --> 00:05:34.234
So, we actually got you
a giant basket.

00:05:34.234 --> 00:05:37.400
full of duck sauce here.
This is for you.

00:05:37.400 --> 00:05:39.300
This is for you.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:39.300 --> 00:05:42.000
Romeo Santos, everybody!

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:45.467
"Fórmula, Vol. 3" is available
right now!

00:05:45.467 --> 00:05:47.601
Romeo's performing
for us after the break.

00:05:47.601 --> 00:05:49.501
Come on back, everybody.

